# Sentinel - ML/DL Network Intrusion Detection System

![Sentinel](assets/icons/sentinel-banner.png)

## Overview

Sentinel is an advanced Network Intrusion Detection System (NIDS) powered by Machine Learning and Deep Learning algorithms. It monitors network traffic across 10 websites, detects intrusions in real-time, and provides comprehensive analytics through an intuitive dashboard.

## Features

### 🧠 ML/DL Detection Engine
- Deep Neural Network for real-time intrusion detection
- Multiple detection algorithms (Anomaly, Signature, Heuristic, Behavioral)
- Ensemble voting for higher accuracy
- Continuous learning with incremental training
- 98.7% detection accuracy

### 📊 12 Real-time Graphs
- Attack type distribution
- Severity levels
- Daily and hourly patterns
- Source analysis
- Confidence metrics

### 🔄 10 Website Swiper
- Swipe/click navigation
- Touch support
- Keyboard shortcuts
- Individual site analytics

### 📈 Log Management
- Yearly, Monthly, Weekly, Day-wise views
- Attack type filtering
- Severity classification
- ML confidence scores
- Difference tracking

### 📄 Reporting
- Automatic report generation
- PDF download
- Threat summary
- ML model metrics

### 🔗 Firebase Integration
- Real-time data sync
- Cloud storage
- Multi-device support
- Offline fallback

## Installation

### Prerequisites
- Node.js (v14+)
- Firebase account (optional)

### Steps

1. Clone the repository:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/sentinel-ids.git
